    "name": "policed-uplink-default-width",
    "description": "The regression for #663. Scenario 15's link - a 10 Mbit/s token-bucket policer with no queue, at 100 ms - carrying the #483 baseline's workload at the SHIPPED upload defaults: sixteen 20 MiB objects, eight in flight, each sent as 8 MiB parts four at a time. Before #663 this committed nothing: two dozen part uploads shared the policed link, each got about 11 KB/s, an 8 MiB part needed far longer than the fixed 300 s request deadline, and every attempt was cut and re-sent from its first byte until every batch failed. The run asserts the outcome rather than recording it: require_all_committed fails it (exit 6) unless every object commits. Read its goodput against the policer's 10 Mbit/s token rate; the iperf3 probe's number is recorded but not gated, as in scenario 15. Requires the netem stack, docker compose -f benchmarks/docker-compose.benchmark.yml --profile netem --profile containerized up -d, and unshapes the middlebox when it ends. One run takes about twenty minutes.",
